.SH NAME
polaric-signcert \- Issue (signn) a certificate request 
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B polaric-signcert
.br

.SH DESCRIPTION
If a signing service (CA) is available and the polaric-certauth-client is installed and correctly configured, this command 
can be used to get a signed certificate (by using the CSR generated by the polaric-newcert command). The resulting certificate
is placed in /etc/polaric-webapp/ssl, replacing the earlier (possibly self-signed) certificate. 

The signing service should be an instance of polaric-certauth-server and the client should be configured to use this, setting
the URL and the API key correcly to get access. 

If the credentials are wrong or the polaric-certauth-client is not installed, this command will have no effect. 
.PP
